# PROJECT RULES & CONSTRAINTS

## 1. FILE MANAGEMENT POLICY (STRICT)
- DO NOT create new files or folders unless explicitly approved.
- ALWAYS modify and refactor existing files within the current directory structure.
- If a task strictly requires creating a new file, STOP immediately and ask for user confirmation first. Explain why a new file is required and wait for approval.

## 2. CODING STANDARDS
- Follow TypeScript best practices with explicit types (avoid using `any`).
- Use existing project conventions, folder patterns, and naming standards.
- Prefer updating existing controllers, services, and routes directly.

## 3. RESPONSE LANGUAGE & STYLE
- Understand and respond to instructions in Khmer and English technical terms seamlessly.
- Keep responses concise, direct, and focused on modified lines of code.